\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_comment_hygiene.py\tD\tscripts/check_comment_hygiene.py::<module>-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py:2-22\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py:2-8\targparse --help; Reject rot-prone historical prose in Python comments and docstrings. A SHA-like token, run ID, or dated incident narrative needs a durable ticket ID or alias, ADR ID, or ``context:\tPASS\t184\t59\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_comment_hygiene.py\tC\tscripts/check_comment_hygiene.py::comment-8-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py:88-93\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py:74-76\tPython documentation; A store alias is 3 lowercase hyphenated words, outside path/filename context. Reject neighboring separators or a file extension; sentence-final punctuation remains valid (ticket b0\tPASS\t73\t27\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py\tD\tscripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py::<module>-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:2-27\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:2-8\targparse --help; Enforce the 50-column subject and 72-column body commit-message convention. Gerrit preserves authored newlines. Do not wrap trailers, fenced or indented code, long unbreakable toke\tPASS\t205\t47\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py\tC\tscripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py::comment-4-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:49-54\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:30-31\tPython documentation; Atomic tokens contain a scheme, path separator, or long structured identifier segments; plain character runs are wrappable prose.\tPASS\t86\t20\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py\tC\tscripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py::comment-5-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:58-62\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:35-36\tPython documentation; Exempt a line only when one unsplittable token exceeds the limit and its short lead-in fits. Extra prose can move to another line.\tPASS\t76\t25\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py\tC\tscripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py::comment-6-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:67-70\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:41-42\tPython documentation; URLs, paths, and structured identifiers can be atomic; bare hex runs are not. The text before an atomic token must fit separately.\tPASS\t56\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\tD\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py::<module>-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:2-72\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:2-19\targparse --help; Shrink-only per-symbol Ruff C901 complexity gate (story c9f7). ``pyproject.toml`` supplies the McCabe threshold (15). Qualified symbol keys in ``.github/complexity-baseline.json`` \tPASS\t554\t147\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\tD\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py::run_scanner-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:131-139\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:78-79\tPython documentation; Run uncached Ruff C901 JSON census using the configured threshold. Parse exit 0/1; missing Ruff, exit >=2, invalid JSON, or non-C901 output raises ScannerError.\tPASS\t78\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\tD\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py::build_symbol_index-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:177-183\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:117-118\tPython documentation; Index function/async-function qualified names by line and name column. Lambdas are excluded; columns distinguish same-line definitions.\tPASS\t43\t16\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\tD\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py::render_violation_details-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:410-418\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:345-346\tPython documentation; Return sorted new-score/threshold and increased-score/ceiling lines after a failing summary; stale-only checks add none.\tPASS\t78\t14\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\tD\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py::lock_against_base-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:489-501\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:417-417\tPython documentation; Report newly added or raised ceilings against the base. Removed or lowered entries pass.\tPASS\t55\t14\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\tD\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py::_base_commit_for_comparison-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:525-538\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:441-443\tPython documentation; Use merge-base(main, HEAD) so later main reductions do not penalize an unchanged branch. If unavailable, compare against main's stricter tip and fail closed (bug humble-cinnamoned-\tPASS\t157\t25\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\tD\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py::_fetch_base_ceilings_from_main-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:576-588\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:481-483\tPython documentation; Fetch canonical GitHub main by explicit URL, then parse the merge-base ceilings. A missing baseline on main returns None; missing repository, fetch, or parse failure raises LockFet\tPASS\t117\t27\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\tC\tscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py::comment-11-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:597-599\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:492-493\tPython documentation; Fetch enough history for merge-base; depth 1 cannot distinguish a branch ceiling raise from a later reduction on main (bug humble-cinnamoned-mussel).\tPASS\t41\t23\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_config_ownership.py\tD\tscripts/check_config_ownership.py::<module>-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_config_ownership.py:2-18\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_config_ownership.py:2-9\tPython documentation; Offline AST gate for ambient configuration and credential ownership. Only approved composition roots and provider boundaries may read environment, load config, read credentials, re\tPASS\t121\t59\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_config_ownership.py\tC\tscripts/check_config_ownership.py::comment-3-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_config_ownership.py:39-44\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_config_ownership.py:30-31\tPython documentation; Approved composition-root basenames own ambient env/config reads; findings fire only below the relevant seam.\tPASS\t39\t16\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_config_ownership.py\tC\tscripts/check_config_ownership.py::comment-4-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_config_ownership.py:49-52\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_config_ownership.py:36-37\tPython documentation; The raw-input and owned-resolver halves share a composition root, so both basenames must be approved after the split (story 1a33).\tPASS\t49\t22\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_config_reads.py\tD\tscripts/check_config_reads.py::<module>-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_config_reads.py:2-32\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_config_reads.py:2-10\tPython documentation; Require a real read of each ``_config_schema.py`` dataclass field. An attribute load counts only when its receiver resolves to the declaring schema class. Resolve section attribute\tPASS\t239\t79\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_config_reads.py\tD\tscripts/check_config_reads.py::_check_marker-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_config_reads.py:104-109\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_config_reads.py:78-79\tPython documentation; Return (found, stripped pointer) for a # read-via: marker on this or the preceding line; otherwise (False, '').\tPASS\t48\t18\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_config_reads.py\tD\tscripts/check_config_reads.py::ticket_pointer_reports-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_config_reads.py:447-456\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_config_reads.py:417-418\tPython documentation; Report, without failing, each # read-via: pointer to a rebar ticket so those exceptions remain visible for review.\tPASS\t109\t18\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_config_reads.py\tC\tscripts/check_config_reads.py::comment-4-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_config_reads.py:53-58\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_config_reads.py:31-32\tPython documentation; Recognize grouped short or full rebar ticket IDs in read-via pointers. Their justification can expire when the ticket closes, so report them.\tPASS\t77\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py\tD\tscripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py::_git_tracked_relatives-d\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:184-189\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:167-167\tPython documentation; Return tracked and nonignored untracked paths, or None outside a usable git repository.\tPASS\t52\t13\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py\tC\tscripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py::comment-3-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:24-30\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:24-26\tPython documentation; In git roots, use git's tracked/nonignored list. Only the non-git fallback needs exclusions; a duplicate denylist would drift past ignored worktrees or scratch and flood lint (bug \tPASS\t102\t31\tPASS\tPASS\tresume-group03-20261023\r\ntaurine-tardy-kite\tscripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py\tC\tscripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py::comment-4-c\t91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a:scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:45-48\t72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62:scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:41-42\tPython documentation; This frozen, scrubbed ticket-prose fixture tests the DC renderer. Rewording captured data would falsify its contract.\tPASS\t45\t18\tPASS\tPASS\tre